<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the `glslang` project. Specifically, the `glslang::TSymbolTable::insert` function does not handle the case where it is called on an empty symbol table (i.e., when no scope has been pushed). This leads to an out-of-bounds access when `currentLevel()` returns -1.

A potential fix would be to add a check at the beginning of `glslang::TSymbolTable::insert` to ensure that the symbol table is not empty before proceeding.

The fuzz driver is correctly using the `glslang` API as intended. However, to avoid this crash and continue fuzzing deeper, the fuzz driver could be modified to push a scope onto the symbol table before inserting the custom struct symbol. This can be done by calling `symbolTable.push()` before `symbolTable.insert()`.
</crash-analysis>

